\[\left|\sum_{i=1}^{3}\alpha_{i}\mathbf{p}_{i}\right|_{m,\kappa}\leqslant C_{7} \sigma^{m}h_{\kappa}^{k-m}|\mathbf{v}|_{k,\,\lambda_{\kappa}}.\]

Then with another application of (2.11), we derive:

\[|\mathbf{v}-\pi_{h}\mathbf{v}|_{m,\kappa}\leqslant C_{8}\sigma^{m}h^{k-m}| \mathbf{v}|_{k,\,\lambda_{\kappa}},\ \ \ \ \ m=0,\,1,\ \ \ \ k=1,\,2.\]

But the regularity of \(\mathscr{T}_{h}\) implies that the maximum number of occurrences of a given triangle \(\kappa\) in the sets \(\lambda_{\kappa}\) is bounded by a fixed constant \(M\) independent of \(h\) and \(\kappa\). Hence

\[\left(\sum_{\kappa\,\in\,\mathscr{T}_{h}}|\mathbf{v}|_{k,\,\lambda_{\kappa}}^ {2}\right)^{1/2}\leqslant M|\mathbf{v}|_{k,\,\Omega}\]

and therefore

\[|\mathbf{v}-\pi_{h}\mathbf{v}|_{m,\,\Omega}\leqslant C_{8}M\sigma^{m}h^{k-m}| \mathbf{v}|_{k,\,\Omega}.\]

In particular, when \(k=m=1\) this establishes the bound (1.20) of Lemma 1.1:

\[|\pi_{h}\mathbf{v}|_{1,\,\Omega}\leqslant(1+C_{8}M\sigma)|\mathbf{v}|_{1,\, \Omega}\ \ \ \ \ \forall\mathbf{v}\in H_{0}^{1}(\Omega)^{2}.\]

And when \(k=2\) and \(m=1\) this yields Hypothesis H1 with \(l=1\). 

Finally, Hypothesis H2 is a direct consequence of Lemma A.5 for the \(L^{2}\)-projection \(\rho_{h}\) onto \(Q_{h}\):

\[\|q-\rho_{h}q\|_{0,\,\Omega}\leqslant Ch|q|_{1,\,\Omega}\ \ \ \ \ \forall q\in H^{1}(\Omega).\] (2.13)

Since all the assumptions of Theorems 1.8 and 1.9 are satisfied, the following convergence result is established for our first-order scheme.

**Theorem 2.1**.: _Suppose \(\Omega\) is a bounded, plane polygon. Let the solution \((\mathbf{u},p)\) of the Stokes problem satisfy:_

\[\mathbf{u}\in[H^{2}(\Omega)\cap H_{0}^{1}(\Omega)]^{2},\ \ \ \ \ p\in H^{1}(\Omega)\cap L_{0}^{2}(\Omega)\]

_and let the spaces \(\bar{X}_{h}\) and \(\bar{M}_{h}\) be defined by (2.3) and (2.4) respectively. If the family of triangulations \(\mathscr{T}_{h}\) is regular then the solution \((\mathbf{u}_{h},p_{h})\) of (1.39) satisfies the error estimate:_

\[|\mathbf{u}-\mathbf{u}_{h}|_{1,\,\Omega}+\|p-p_{h}\|_{0,\,\Omega}\leqslant C_{ 1}h(|\mathbf{u}|_{2,\,\Omega}+|p|_{1,\,\Omega}).\] (2.14)

_In addition, if \(\Omega\) is convex, we have_

\[\|\mathbf{u}-\mathbf{u}_{h}\|_{0,\,\Omega}\leqslant C_{2}h^{2}(|\mathbf{u}|_{ 2,\,\Omega}+|p|_{1,\,\Omega}).\] (2.15)

_Remark 2.2_.: Both upper bounds are stated in terms of seminorms of \(\mathbf{u}\) and \(p\) whereas the estimates of Theorems 1.8 and 1.9 involve full norms in their right-hand sides. This slight refinement is due to the fact that both (2.11) and (2.13) are formulated with seminorms only.
